!! Show a text file in a desktop window, rendering markdown as formatted prose and anything else as plain text, and re-read it whenever it changes.
!!
!! Run with `allspeak mdshow`. This is a desktop application rather than a browser one, so the window comes from the Python runtime's graphics domain rather than from Webson. The file to watch is named in `.mdshow.conf`; when no name is there, and whenever Select File is pressed, the operating system's own chooser supplies one, and the window is titled with the path of whichever file is being watched.

!   mdshow.allspeak

    script Mdshow

!! @hash 00cd2d7c
!!!

!! Load the desktop graphics domain, which supplies the window, the native file chooser, the two panels and the Qt event loop this script is built on.

    use graphics


!! @hash 857a3262
!!!

!! Declare the widgets the script builds.
!!
!! Widget variables must exist before `create` can instantiate them. `DocPanel` is a `mdpanel` — a read-only panel whose text setter converts markdown to HTML, so a markdown file reaches the screen as formatted prose. `SourceView` is a `multiline` built `readonly`, the plain-text counterpart that every other kind of file goes to. Neither is given `cols`/`rows`, so both expand to fill the window, and only one of them is ever visible. `OpenDlg` is a `file` dialog: the OS's own chooser, whose result is the path the user picked.

    window MainWindow
    layout Panel
    layout TopRow
    pushbutton OpenButton
    mdpanel DocPanel
    multiline SourceView
    dialog OpenDlg


!! @hash f4746f30
!!!

!! Declare the state shared between the startup path, the poller and the event handlers.
!!
!! `Conf` is the saved configuration — window geometry plus the watched file — `HaveGeometry` records whether a usable geometry was found, and `WinX`/`WinY`/`WinW`/`WinH` carry it to the `create` call. `Watched` is the path being watched and `ShownFile` the path the panel is currently showing; `Contents` is the text just read and `Shown` the text on screen. `Chosen` receives the chooser's result, and `Lower` holds the lower-cased path used to spot a markdown extension.

    dictionary Conf
    variable HaveGeometry
    variable WinX
    variable WinY
    variable WinW
    variable WinH
    variable Watched
    variable ShownFile
    variable Contents
    variable Shown
    variable Chosen
    variable Lower


!! @hash 00e7bcbd
!!!

!! Start from a known state before anything reads it.
!!
!! `reset` empties the dictionary and `clear` sets the boolean false — a flag must be initialised before it can be tested. Leaving `Shown` and `ShownFile` empty means the poller's first pass always renders, even if the watched file is itself empty.

    reset Conf
    clear HaveGeometry
    put empty into Watched
    put empty into ShownFile
    put empty into Shown
    put empty into Contents


!! @hash 93d4fce1
!!!

!! Recover the window geometry and the file to watch, both saved by a previous run.
!!
!! Relative paths resolve against this script's own folder, so `.mdshow.conf` is read from the project directory however the script is launched. On a first run the config file does not exist and the `on failure` clause clears `HaveGeometry`, so the script falls back to a default size and lets Qt centre the window; `Watched` stays empty and the chooser runs instead.
!!
!! All four geometry values are required: a truncated or hand-edited file is ignored rather than half-applied, which is why this is one four-way test instead of four reads of entries that might not be there. The `file` entry is independent of them — a path named there is watched whatever the geometry says.

    if file `.mdshow.conf` exists
    begin
        load Conf from `.mdshow.conf`
        on failure clear HaveGeometry
        if Conf has entry `x` and Conf has entry `y` and Conf has entry `width` and Conf has entry `height`
        begin
            put entry `x` of Conf into WinX
            put entry `y` of Conf into WinY
            put entry `width` of Conf into WinW
            put entry `height` of Conf into WinH
            set HaveGeometry
        end
        if Conf has entry `file`
            put entry `file` of Conf into Watched
    end


!! @hash 8abab847
!!!

!! Hand control to Qt.
!!
!! Everything after this point runs in slices on the runtime's flush timer rather than in one go, so the window becomes interactive while the rest of the setup is still finishing.

    init graphics


!! @hash d57326f7
!!!

!! Build the interface — button row, panels, window, chooser.
!!
!! The layouts are populated before the window exists because `create … layout Panel` attaches the vertical one immediately. `SourceView` is hidden as it is built so that only the markdown panel takes up space until the first render decides which of the two the watched file needs. The window is created titled `mdshow`, the name it keeps until a file is settled on. Only the window's geometry differs between runs, and it can only be set at `create` time, which is why the values recovered above are read here instead of applied afterwards.

    create Panel type QVBoxLayout
    create TopRow type QHBoxLayout
    create OpenButton text `Select File`
    add OpenButton to TopRow
    add stretch to TopRow
    add TopRow to Panel

    create DocPanel
    create SourceView readonly
    add DocPanel to Panel
    add SourceView to Panel
    hide SourceView

    if HaveGeometry
        create MainWindow title `mdshow` at WinX WinY size WinW WinH
    else
        create MainWindow title `mdshow` size 800 600

    set the layout of MainWindow to Panel
    create OpenDlg on MainWindow type file title `Select a file`


!! @hash ef8c5446
!!!

!! Register the close and click handlers while the window and the button still exist to receive them.
!!
!! The close handler is the last point at which the position can be read back, so it has to be in place before the window is shown.

    on close MainWindow go to SaveState
    on click OpenButton go to SelectClick


!! @hash 5bdaac32
!!!

!! Show the window, name it after the file if one was remembered, then start the watcher.
!!
!! A remembered file is what the window is titled with; with no file, the chooser runs and titles the window as soon as a path is accepted, and a cancel leaves the `mdshow` it was created with. The chooser runs before the poller is forked so that a first run does not spend its opening second rendering the empty state. The main flow ends at `stop`: the window, the chooser and the poller are separate threads that keep running under the event loop, and the program exits when the last window closes.

    show MainWindow
    if Watched is empty
        gosub ChooseFile
    else
        set the title of MainWindow to Watched
    fork to PollFile
    stop


!! @hash 1fd68d4d
!!!

!! Re-read the watched file once a second and re-render only when something has changed.
!!
!! The `wait` is what lets the rest of the program run between passes — a loop without it would starve the UI, since threads are cooperative and yield only at `wait`, blocking I/O or `stop`. It sits outside every `gosub` on purpose: threads share one return stack, so a label that suspended between `gosub` and `return` would hand its frames back to whichever thread ran next.

PollFile:
    gosub Refresh
    wait 1 second
    go to PollFile


!! @hash 9c253f0f
!!!

!! Read the watched file and render it if the file or its text has changed.
!!
!! An empty `Watched` is the state reached by cancelling the chooser: the panel says so rather than going blank. The `file … exists` test keeps a missing file from raising an error every second, and comparing `ShownFile` as well as `Shown` is what makes choosing a different file redraw even when both files hold the same text.

Refresh:
    if Watched is empty
        put `No file selected.` into Contents
    else
    begin
        if file Watched exists
        begin
            load Contents from Watched
            on failure put `Could not read ` cat Watched cat `.` into Contents
        end
        else
            put Watched cat ` is not there.` into Contents
    end
    if Contents is not Shown or Watched is not ShownFile
        gosub Render
    return


!! @hash 05bf086b
!!!

!! Write the current text to whichever panel matches the kind of file.
!!
!! A markdown file goes to the `mdpanel`, which renders it as formatted prose; anything else goes to the read-only plain-text field exactly as it was read. The two widgets take turns in one slot of the layout, so the one not in use is hidden rather than removed.

Render:
    put lowercase Watched into Lower
    if Lower ends with `.md` or Lower ends with `.markdown`
    begin
        hide SourceView
        show DocPanel
        set the text of DocPanel to Contents
    end
    else
    begin
        hide DocPanel
        show SourceView
        set the text of SourceView to Contents
    end
    put Contents into Shown
    put Watched into ShownFile
    return


!! @hash ad3c54a8
!!!

!! Ask the user for a file with the system chooser and adopt the choice.
!!
!! `show` blocks in the native chooser until it closes, and reading the result afterwards gives the chosen path, or an empty string if the user cancelled — so an empty `Chosen` leaves the watched file alone. An accepted path is written to the configuration straight away, so it survives even a run that is killed rather than closed, and retitles the window, whose caption is the only place the full path is on show.

ChooseFile:
    show OpenDlg
    put OpenDlg into Chosen
    if Chosen is empty
        return
    put Chosen into Watched
    set the title of MainWindow to Watched
    set entry `file` of Conf to Watched
    save prettify Conf to `.mdshow.conf`
    gosub Refresh
    return


!! @hash e2f12dc9
!!!

!! Handle a click on the Select File button.
!!
!! The button's only job is to reopen the chooser, so the handler is the shared `ChooseFile` step followed by the `stop` that ends an event handler's thread.

SelectClick:
    gosub ChooseFile
    stop


!! @hash 282f0743
!!!

!! Save the window's size and position, and the watched file, as the program shuts down.
!!
!! The handler runs inside the close event, before Qt destroys the window and before the runtime ends the program as its last window goes — so it runs straight through to `stop` with nothing in between that could yield. The JSON is written pretty-printed to keep the file readable by hand.

SaveState:
    put the x of MainWindow into WinX
    put the y of MainWindow into WinY
    put the width of MainWindow into WinW
    put the height of MainWindow into WinH
    set entry `x` of Conf to WinX
    set entry `y` of Conf to WinY
    set entry `width` of Conf to WinW
    set entry `height` of Conf to WinH
    set entry `file` of Conf to Watched
    save prettify Conf to `.mdshow.conf`
    stop


!! @hash 9574daa9
!!!
